# github_keys renders from `gitHubKeys .git.username`. With an empty username,
# chezmoi's underlying client falls back to the *authenticated user* endpoint
# (/user/keys instead of /users/<name>/keys), which needs a user token and 403s
# under the GITHUB_TOKEN a workflow gets -- failing the whole apply. Skipping
# the file outright is right anyway: with no username there are no keys to
# fetch, and rendering an empty ~/.ssh/github_keys serves nobody.
#
# `dig` rather than `.git.username` so a config without a [data.git] table at
# all renders instead of dying on "map has no entry for key" -- this file gates
# every target, so a hard failure here takes the whole apply down with it.
{{ if not (dig "git" "username" "" .) }}
.ssh/github_keys
{{ end }}
